/-
OnBytes/Key/TestRecordToyValues.lean: the intermediate values of the check of the toy key file of
OnBytes/Entry/RecordToyFiles.lean agree with the programs'.

The programs write 106 field elements that their verifier computes on its way through the honest
key's three chains: blocks/frame/handover_files.cpp writes them beside the file, as key.targets.tsv,
each with a name. Here they are compared, name by name and element by element, in their order, with
what the three chains' blocks note in their runs on the same bytes. The blocks, their starts and the
views are those of Key.keyRefusal (OnBytes/Key/File.lean) and Proof.tailRefusal
(OnBytes/Proof/Tail.lean), spelled again here, since no function of the library returns what a key's
blocks note.

Every test is checked when the file compiles. The program does not import this file.

Not claimed. No theorem. One honest file. That a value which is noted is the value on which the
decision hangs is not shown. Nothing on soundness, completeness or hiding.
-/
import OnBytes.Key.TestRecordToy

namespace OnBytes.Entry.RecordToy

/-- What the blocks of the key's three chains note on the honest key: each name with the element's
coordinates. -/
def keyNoted : Option (List (String × UInt64 × UInt64 × UInt64)) := do
  let k ← chains
  let p := k.oneTime
  let (table, j) ← (Key.readTable p.lin.fold.index p.given.cfg keyFile).toOption
  let r ← (Key.readKey k table keyFile j).fromStart.toOption
  let q := Key.tailPublic k table
  let real ← (Proof.judge "" (Key.oneTime p) (Key.startOf p) r.first.view).toOption
  let shared := Proof.sharedBlock q.lin r.key
  let end2 ← (Proof.judge "" shared (Proof.sharedStart q) r.shared.view).toOption
  let second := Proof.secondBlock q.lin real.lin (end2.goesOn r.shared)
  let notes := (Key.oneTime p).notesOn (Key.startOf p) r.first.view ++
    shared.notesOn (Proof.sharedStart q) r.shared.view ++
    second.notesOn (Proof.secondStart q real r.first) r.second.view
  pure (notes.toList.map fun x => (x.1, x.2.c0, x.2.c1, x.2.c2))

